cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CarboSeis, please cite it and CarboKitten.jl."
title: "CarboSeis: a workflow for constructing seismic models of carbonate platforms from CarboKitten forward simulations"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-23
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23608277
repository-code: "https://github.com/yupenglee2006-ui/CarboSeis"
abstract: >-
  CarboSeis constructs a seismic model of a carbonate formation simulated with CarboKitten.jl.
  From a scenario file that holds the petrophysical description of the formation it derives
  texture, porosity, pore structure and elastic properties for every layer, embeds the carbonate
  body in water, overburden and onlapping fill, and outputs post-stack synthetic seismic sections
  by one-dimensional convolution or point-spread-function imaging.
keywords:
  - carbonate platform
  - stratigraphic forward modelling
  - rock physics
  - synthetic seismic
  - CarboKitten
authors:
